@ekrctb: You're correct that the sequence `Finished -> Began` is the biggest one of concern.

I wanted to maintain consistency to make sure that only one event ever happens per frame. For example, consider my tests where I schedule a removal on an intermediate container somewhere between the HOCs and the buffer. With your implementation, two events happen per frame - transfer/begin + finish.

But I've adopted your implementation anyway - I suppose keeping it simple is best for now, and we can go back to my previous implementation if this ever comes up as a problem.
